      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KIWI LISMORE (5) jumped from box 4 last time and ran away with an impressive win scoring by 6 lengths at Geelong in a handy 25.62. Has the squeeze box to overcome and will need the breaks early. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card in scoring last start. Will go close again if runs up to latest. YALE TURN (3) goes very well at the distance with two wins and a placing from six starts. Hit the frame latest (31.37) when third at The Meadows in a Restricted WIN. With even luck and a clean start should be around the money. STIDHAM KANSAS (1) is worth forgiving last start after finishing fourth (30.71) from Box 4 at The Meadows over 525m. Cannot be underestimated. MIDWAY CENTRAL (2) has definite claims at his first try at this circuit.",
